# Fueled Workflow Rules

This project uses **Fueled** — a documentation-driven development system.

## Core Principle

**PRD-first development:** Every feature must have an approved PRD before implementation begins.

## Directory Structure

```
requirements/          # PRDs organized by domain/epic/feature
├── index.md          # Root requirements index
└── [domain]/
    └── [epic]/
        └── [feature].prd.md

.planning/            # State, roadmap, phase plans
├── STATE.md          # Project state tracking
├── ROADMAP.md        # Implementation roadmap (when created)
├── phases/           # Phase execution plans
└── todos/            # Pending and completed todos

.fueled/              # System configuration
├── config.json       # Settings and paths
├── STATUS.md         # Master status dashboard
├── research/         # Research artifacts
└── exports/          # Generated stakeholder docs
```

## Workflow Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `/fueled:status` | View project dashboard |
| `/fueled:new-prd [domain/epic/feature]` | Create new PRD |
| `/fueled:review-prd` | Check PRD completeness |
| `/fueled:approve-prd` | Mark PRD approved |
| `/fueled:generate-stakeholder <type>` | Generate stakeholder doc |
| `/fueled:create-roadmap` | Create implementation roadmap |
| `/fueled:plan-phase` | Plan implementation phase |
| `/fueled:execute-phase` | Execute planned phase |
| `/fueled:validate-build` | Validate code matches PRD |

## Before Writing Code

1. Check if a PRD exists for this feature
2. If no PRD, create one with `/fueled:new-prd`
3. Get PRD approved before implementation
4. Follow the phase plan for implementation order

## Session Start

Always read `.planning/STATE.md` first to understand:
- Current position (phase, plan)
- Recent decisions
- Pending todos
- Where to resume

## After Completing Work

Update `.planning/STATE.md` with:
- New position
- Decisions made
- Any blockers discovered
